$431,864 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 31K people. Revenue per employee of $437K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 37%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $69K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $33K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["DoorDash, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $73.2B market cap on $13.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +4.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -19% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $2.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.60\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -562.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 184% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.8365859279084567},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $17.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Which Businesses Lifted DoorDash (NASDAQ:DASH) Revenue This Quarter?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/which-businesses-lifted-doordash-nasdaqdash-revenue-this-quarter","date":"2026-11-26","